# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PRIVATE BY DEFAULT — everything below never leaves this machine.
#
# THE RULE: working communications and any notes dropped into the project
# folder are private. Do not rely on remembering to add each new file here —
# put it in internal/ and it is private structurally.
#
#   internal/   ← the ONLY place private material belongs. Anything in it is
#                 ignored, including subdirectories created later.
#
# What lives there: the working journal (DTB_CHANGELOG-internal.md), rolling
# state (RESUME-HERE.md), handoffs, upstreaming notes, raw analysis transcripts,
# the eDP series, decompiled test DTBs, diagnostic-only patches, hardware
# evidence captures, build logs, dtdiff output, and DRAFT emails/bug reports.
#
# ⛔ Draft communications are private until sent. They live in internal/ and
#    must never be committed.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
internal/

# CLAUDE.md must stay at the repo root — Claude Code loads it from there — so
# it cannot move into internal/ and is ignored by name instead.
CLAUDE.md

# Hardware/firmware captures are private wherever they land (post-2026-07-31
# MSDM leak). Belt and braces alongside internal/.
docs/evidence/
**/*.dat
**/*msdm*

